<Information title="About" description="An independent guide by Optimum Tech to choosing tools for Elixir applications.">
<p>elixir.menu is an independent guide by <a href="https://optimum.ba">Optimum Tech</a> to choosing tools for Elixir applications. Start with your application type, explore a preferred Phoenix and LiveView web stack, and choose optional libraries by feature.</p>
<p>Each recommendation explains why a tool fits and when to choose something else. Use the guide as a starting point for the needs of your application.</p>
<h2>A reference, not an installer</h2>
<p>The guide is independent of the Elixir and Phoenix teams. It is not a framework or an installer, and the complete set of optional libraries has not been tested as one integrated distribution.</p>
<p><a href="/">Browse the menu</a> or read the <a href="/setup.md">Phoenix setup guide</a>. The <a href="https://github.com/optimumBA/elixir.menu">source and editorial content</a> use Apache 2.0; linked projects retain their own licenses.</p>
</Information>
